⍝ Multiply.tc
⍝ ═══════════

⍝@ test4.

      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ Precond: A and B numeric
      ⍝ inv: A×B ←→ B×A   (× is commutative, even when the product
      ⍝ overflows and is promoted to float)
      A ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      (A×B) ≡ B×A
1
      A ← ⎕RVAL 2 (3 4) (,0 0 1 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 2 (3 4) (,0 0 1 0 0)
      (A×B) ≡ B×A
1

      ⍝ Precond: Big sits at the int64 boundary and N is a small
      ⍝ integer ≥2, so Big×N always crosses the conservative LARGE_INT
      ⍝ threshold and is promoted to float (IntCell::bif_multiply_ii());
      ⍝ N is small enough that dividing it back out of the float
      ⍝ product is exact
      ⍝ inv: Big ←→ (Big×N)÷N
      N ← 2+8∣|⎕RVAL 0
      Big ← 9223372036854775807
      Big ≡ (Big×N)÷N
1
      Big ← ¯9223372036854775807
      Big ≡ (Big×N)÷N
1
